WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.089
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.089 --> 00:00:04.004
<v Examiner>Define evidence-based practice,

3
00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:07.649
<v Examiner>and discuss why it's a professional requirement for nurses,

4
00:00:07.649 --> 00:00:09.687
<v Examiner>including the levels of evidence.

5
00:00:10.137 --> 00:00:14.867
Evidence-based practice combines three things: the best research evidence,

6
00:00:14.867 --> 00:00:19.598
clinical expertise, and the patient's values, to improve patient outcomes.

7
00:00:19.598 --> 00:00:24.775
It's a shift in healthcare culture away from basing decisions on opinion and past

8
00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:27.268
practice, toward research and evidence.

9
00:00:27.718 --> 00:00:28.851
Why it's required.

10
00:00:28.851 --> 00:00:31.556
Pou four of the Registered Nurse Standards,

11
00:00:31.556 --> 00:00:34.828
pūkengatanga and evidence-informed nursing practice,

12
00:00:34.828 --> 00:00:40.240
requires nurses to use clinical skills and critical thinking informed by high-quality,

13
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:43.071
current evidence, to give safe, quality care.

14
00:00:43.071 --> 00:00:48.671
And principle four of the Code of Conduct says keep your knowledge and skills up to date,

15
00:00:48.671 --> 00:00:51.503
and reflect on your practice with colleagues.

16
00:00:51.503 --> 00:00:55.970
Discuss means link it: evidence protects patients from outdated habits,

17
00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.361
and it's how practice keeps improving.

18
00:00:58.811 --> 00:01:01.961
The levels of evidence, weakest to strongest.

19
00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.011
Expert opinion.

20
00:01:03.011 --> 00:01:04.411
Qualitative studies.

21
00:01:04.411 --> 00:01:05.881
Quantitative studies.

22
00:01:05.881 --> 00:01:08.191
Non-randomised controlled trials.

23
00:01:08.191 --> 00:01:10.220
Randomised controlled trials.

24
00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:12.670
And at the top, systematic reviews.

25
00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.750
So the highest level is a systematic review.

26
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.666
How to do it: the first step is to formulate a clinical question,

27
00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:25.201
then search the databases, like C I N A H L, the Cochrane Library,

28
00:01:25.201 --> 00:01:26.919
Joanna Briggs and PubMed.

29
00:01:26.919 --> 00:01:32.072
The primary goal of evidence-based practice is to improve patient outcomes.

30
00:01:32.522 --> 00:01:37.634
Evidence-based practice: best research, clinical expertise and patient values,

31
00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:38.945
to improve outcomes.

32
00:01:38.945 --> 00:01:41.894
Required by pou four and the Code of Conduct.

33
00:01:41.894 --> 00:01:47.007
Evidence from weakest to strongest: expert opinion, qualitative, quantitative,

34
00:01:47.007 --> 00:01:52.447
non-randomised trials, randomised controlled trials, systematic reviews at the top.

35
00:01:52.447 --> 00:01:55.199
First step: formulate a clinical question.
